here's a basic script for a first-person character in unity, in C#

```C#
using UnityEngine;

public class FirstPersonController : MonoBehaviour
{
    public float moveSpeed = 5.0f;
    public float jumpForce = 10.0f;
    private Rigidbody rb;

    void Start()
    {
        rb = GetComponent<Rigidbody>();
    }

    void Update()
    {
        float horizontal = Input.GetAxis("Horizontal");
        float vertical = Input.GetAxis("Vertical");
        Vector3 movement = new Vector3(horizontal, 0, vertical);
        rb.AddForce(movement * moveSpeed);

        if (Input.GetButtonDown("Jump") && rb.velocity.y == 0)
        {
            rb.AddForce(Vector3.up * jumpForce, ForceMode.Impulse);
        }
    }
}
```

it uses the Horizontal and Vertical inputs for movement, and the Jump button for jumping. the Rigidbody component does the heavy lifting, adding forces to move the character.

this one's great for a quick start, but there's plenty more you might want — smooth turning, crouching, sprinting, physics-based walking, looking around, and a few others. you got a favorite extra? ^^
